From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:18:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(image2): deliver the requested frame end-to-end

- OpenAI gpt-image-2 sizes now respect the documented custom-size rules
  (multiple of 16, 655,360-8,294,400 px). The old table (1024x576, 960x640,
  1008x432, ...) was rejected with HTTP 400, so every non-4:3 frame failed.
- frame_ratio: documented 8% gate (Magic Hour 640x384 is 6.25% off 16:9) and
  a new crop_to_frame() that trims the provider approximation to the exact
  ratio instead of discarding the generation.
- image_render: crop stored output before inserting the asset; drop the dead
  _crop_stored_image_to_ratio helper.
- image2 UI resets an unsupported frame instead of disabling Generate;
  /api/generate rejects unknown frames instead of silently returning 1:1.
- Add frame regression tests and an offline diagnostic script.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
